1:1 COMMENT "# numeric_dissect.z -- compile-time dissection of a numeric-value generic"
1:74 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "# parameter. `match cap` (bare, inside the type) and `match B8.cap` (through a"
2:79 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# name of the instance) both select a code path by the parameter's concrete"
3:76 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "# VALUE at monomorphisation; only the matching arm survives in the generated C"
4:79 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "# (the zerolang analogue of #ifdef over a compile-time constant). An `else`"
5:76 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "# handles the unmatched values."
